#
# Competency question: "Which qualitative analytic properties are there, and by which
# defining law or boundary record is each backed?" This surfaces the machine-audited
# backing edge math:definingLaw over the open math:AnalyticProperty vocabulary: each
# analytic property reports the real first-order logic:Formula defining law that grounds
# it (math:nonAffinity -> math:nonAffinityLaw, math:convexity -> math:convexityLaw,
# math:boundedness -> math:boundednessLaw) or, for the genuinely second-order
# smoothness, the honest recorded logic:expressivenessBoundary math:smoothnessBoundary.
# Read over the merged ontology (no fixture), the answer is exactly the four
# property -> backing pairs. The analysis-charter sibling of
# topological-property-defining-law.rq.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>

SELECT ?property ?backing WHERE {
    ?property a math:AnalyticProperty ;
              math:definingLaw ?backing .
}
ORDER BY ?property ?backing
